-- title:
--   An injective functional on the archimedean continuous H²
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $S$ be a finite set of primes. Consider the archimedean slot of the arithmetic local datum attached to $S$: the index $\mathrm{inl}(())$ of `extArithIndex S` carries the group `archimedeanDecomposition`, a subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ generated by a complex conjugation, and `extArithLoc S (Sum.inl ())` is its inclusion homomorphism `archimedeanLoc` into $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$; neither group nor map depends on $S$. The coefficients are `ofChar` applied to the composite of this inclusion with the mod $p$ cyclotomic character `cycloChar p` of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, namely the one-dimensional representation of the archimedean group on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ obtained by twisting the trivial representation by that character. The assertion is that the continuous second cohomology `continuousH2` of this situation — the quotient of the submodule of two-cocycles `levelCocycles₂` by the part of `levelCoboundaries₂` contained in it — admits a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear map to $\mathbb{Z}/p$ which is injective; equivalently, this cohomology is a $\mathbb{F}_p$-vector space of dimension at most one.
--
--   This records the archimedean invariant map: for the decomposition group at the real place with coefficients in the mod $p$ cyclotomic line, the second continuous cohomology embeds into $\mathbb{F}_p$ (it vanishes for odd $p$ and is one-dimensional for $p=2$, where it is the $2$-torsion of the Brauer group of $\mathbb{R}$). It supplies the archimedean normalisation used by the all-places duality and Selmer-group arguments, and is cited in the construction of global classes of prescribed local restrictions in degree one.
